WEBVTT

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:07.190
We have a follow-up report

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:12.060
from live at the scene of today's armed occupation of the East Asian Economic Federation's Far East trade embassy.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.760
You're the ideal person for the job, Major Kusanagi.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.880
Thank you, Special Adviser Fujimoto.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.750
Our victory is close at hand, Lt. Col. Kurutsu.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.520
I agree, Ambassador Wong.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.360
Our interview is just a formality.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.900
These days AIs and administrators do the deliberations.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.960
Won't this conversation affect the outcome?

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.870
Humans need not be daunted by machines.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:53.150
Your unit aligns perfectly with
 a critical governmental problem.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:06.890
When the war ended, change took the world by storm.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.890
This country is no exception.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:16.570
The war accelerated cyberbrain and prosthetic development.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.450
The cybercrimes resulting from that process are serious,

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.070
but the real problem is more fundamental.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:33.210
The cyberbrain and prosthetics businesses spawned the largest profit-seeking system in history.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:40.800
The massive amount of data now shared in real time has gone beyond what any country can manage.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.740
Even assuming that conglomerates will eliminate all nations and races one day,

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:53.220
the state's role isn't over yet.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.480
Yes.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.940
The anarchic system calling itself the "global economy" will destroy any private financial security,

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.110
which is the foundation of the state.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:05.570
Fall back!

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:25.180
Cyberbrains and prosthetics are the bridge connecting the systems of munitions industry and household economics.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:29.220
Government regulations are meaningless at this point.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:36.940
While no executive organ exists
 which can truly contain the system,

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.890
that doesn't mean it transcends laws established by the state.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:46.300
Systems which break the law must be taken care of directly.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:55.750
Informatization forces us to choose between becoming the system and subordinating ourselves to it.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.750
What we need now...

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.710
...is an executive organ to offensively pass judgment on the system.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:07.590
...is a network to integrate with the system and sort people appropriately.

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:21.020
We recognize you and your organization as an enterprise we should welcome, Lt. Col. Kurutsu.

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:23.990
Anti-terror activities under direct governmental authority.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.000
State-of-the-art cyber investigation.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.900
The power to bring charges for corporate crimes.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.380
Nothing is taboo for your unit.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:33.730
You done yet, Major?

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:34.830
In a few minutes.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.790
What's the sitrep?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.650
One hour into the raid, it's a circus over here.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:46.460
Dammit! It's Ape-Face from Public Security Section 9.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:53.680
Isn't Chief Aramaki the one that requested us?

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:56.390
He wants us working for him.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.390
That doesn't suit our separatist leader.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.030
The ape's assumed authority.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:05.320
What now, Major? Want me to break into Section 9's Net?

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:08.500
I'll negotiate. Just wait for me.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:16.900
The Prime Minister would like to see this incident resolved promptly.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:23.130
And you've just been given the authority to do it.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:27.210
Thank you, sir.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.140
Do you like this country?

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:38.850
Enough to exert my full abilities, at least.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:43.310
The country should work to earn your love, then.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.680
I'll begin immediately.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.190
Oh, and...

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:53.200
Sir?

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.080
Your smile is too perfect.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.660
You don't need to devote so much of your prosthetic memory to it.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:07.630
I've never given a programmed smile, sir.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:13.590
I have no intention of questioning your soul—your Ghost.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.060
I'm heading to the scene.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.220
Good luck.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.720
Ishikawa, information.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:42.280
I see a report from federal council session 320 approving the budget.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.800
Nice work, Major.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:48.910
Get in my lobby.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.270
We're taking this case.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:16.110
Kusanagi.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.030
I didn't expect to see you here.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.490
Did you come to wag your tail 
for our antiquated government?

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.860
And you?

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:28.250
Going to become a corporate 
profit-seeking machine, Kurutsu?

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:31.200
Most of the military is going to be privatized.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.070
This is a war.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:35.470
Side with the losers, and you have no future.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.920
The war is over.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:41.430
I won't let them put a serial number on my Ghost, too.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.430
Everyone is replaceable and expendable.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:51.470
We'll soon find out which of us is the disposable one.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:17.710
ETA seven minutes.

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:19.250
I assume you have my info.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:42.910
Eleven soldiers who opposed downgrading Defense from "Ministry" to "Agency"

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:47.630
have occupied the East Asian Economic Federation's Far East trade embassy.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:52.290
Here are their current positions, backgrounds, and affiliations.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.670
Um...

00:10:55.620 --> 00:11:00.840
All eleven are prosthetized, and two of 'em have heavy-class converted prosthetics.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.910
Nothing the riot police oughta fool with.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:11.940
Out of 42 hostages, 36 are confined in the hall with the bombs.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.850
The others are higher-ups who escaped into the panic room.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:17.270
They're probably the real targets.

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:20.360
If that door opens, we're screwed.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.830
They'll either hole up in there for a year or start staging public executions.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.210
What are their demands?

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:30.170
They want the government to keep the Ministry and suspend military trials.

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:32.290
They didn't ask for their own escape.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:35.640
They just want their own little battlefield.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.760
Execute domination on my signal. We're going in.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.400
Wait, just the <i>seven</i> of us?!

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:46.330
We have a sniper, cyberbrain hacking 
for support, and Logicomas for shields.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.280
The riot police at the perimeter will keep enemy reinforcements away.

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:50.750
You need anything else?

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.100
Seriously?

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:57.020
Guess the rookie can't do anything without a textbook and a necktie.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.830
It must be rough, being the only one with a natural body.

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:03.700
Why not take this chance to go full cyborg?

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:07.590
If you die, I'll call your pretty wife for you.

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:12.160
I can at least collect your last words 
before your cyberbrain's blown away.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:17.130
Call me if you want someone to make your death painless.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:19.400
Screw you jerks!

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.440
Fine, I'll do it and show you all!

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:25.890
You're top-notch parts I collected.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:30.790
If you can't perform anymore, I'll purge you.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:35.850
But most of you would wind up in jail or shot in the back

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.610
if you weren't on my squad.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.610
Don't forget that.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.210
Get in position and prepare to go in.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:48.550
She's calling us machine parts now?

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:54.250
Our naive princess probably meant it as a pep talk.

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:55.960
Downright evil.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.480
Crazy bitch.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:59.210
She's a cruel mistress.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:02.180
It just means she trusts us.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:06.070
<i>Dammit, I seriously might get killed.</i>

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:09.760
We need more personnel to storm them!

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:14.000
Where's Special Forces? Where are the Rangers?!

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.880
<i>Everyone refused to come.</i>

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:20.270
<i>They don't want to shoot their own people to save some foreign war merchants.</i>

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:24.030
Tell them to help these guys by stopping them from committing more crimes!

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.570
Any squads associated with them will be charged with conspiracy!

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:31.290
Pull out the negotiators, Chief.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.750
You're finally here, Major?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.750
Sorry, but you'll need to stand down.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:41.750
Oh, so that suspicious squad budget the council just passed was yours?

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.980
<i>It's not like you to rely on politicians.</i>

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:47.460
I saved myself some hassle by negotiating with the top.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:53.070
<i>"Directly under the Prime Minister" only means something on paper.</i>

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:56.140
<i>I recommend a squad that follows international law.</i>

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:03.000
A "special unit within the international rescue team," I think you said?

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.610
<i>We'd already have one if it weren't for the war.</i>

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:12.280
It would nip crimes in the bud, 
and stop incidents like this before they happened.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:16.620
Nice thought, but I'll take this case over your fantasy squad.

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:19.160
When are you going in?

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:20.330
In 20 seconds.

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:25.220
We'll try not to kill anyone, 
so you'll have something to do afterward.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.190
She's like a kid with a new toy.

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:53.990
Dominate now.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:02.330
Our comm lines just got dominated!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.120
I like a good opponent.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:05.550
Bring it on!

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.980
My sights... She's infiltrated my vision!

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:18.740
Hey, what's wrong?

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.750
Hello!

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:45.150
Bastards!

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.650
Logicomas, protect the hostages.

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.510
Order acknowledged!

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:06.140
Are you my prey?

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:09.590
<i>Move it! Don't give up the hostages!</i>

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:11.590
<i>Do whatever it takes to buy time!</i>

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:13.050
Hello.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.820
See? I contribute.

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.240
Go down, dammit!

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:54.410
Where are you aiming? Don't kill them!

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.680
Don't monitor my vision all the time!

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.830
Break your kill shot habit. The war is over.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:06.480
Tell that to the people still fighting it.

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:13.770
Die!

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.240
Bummer for you.

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:29.080
Guess your conversion was all about might.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:35.200
I bet when you went full cyborg after nearly dying on the field, you felt like you'd become the best you'd ever been.

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:43.330
I did, too.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.980
All done here, Major.

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.030
How's the panic room?

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.950
The door's fine. Two men on the move.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.380
Batou and I will box them in.

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:04.410
Free the hostages and put everyone you've captured in the hall.

00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:10.820
Should we go in, too?

00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:13.040
You like playing the clown?

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:17.630
As long as we beat the central authorities to inspecting the scene, we're fine.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:23.810
Seven people stealing the perps we used 200 to surround...

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:25.510
Now that's entertainment.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:36.900
He's all right, Mr. Prime Minister.

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.410
I'll issue a directive.

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:51.640
Batou?

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:54.420
Major? Where's the enemy?

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.930
Ishikawa, what's going on?

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.020
I was jammed for a second.

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:06.260
There's a twelfth person on the property.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:09.020
A twelfth? Find them!

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:12.430
Look.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.330
Friendly fire?

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.520
Come on, everyone outside!

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:58.490
Something's off.

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:00.190
We're one person short.

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:02.550
There's been some noise on the comm line...

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:16.420
Hey, don't touch those!

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.480
The hostages' cyberbrains are contaminated!

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:31.010
This pattern is...

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:33.020
The false memory virus.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.640
It's Fire-Starter!

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.110
Give them the virtual vaccine!

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:39.270
I thought they were ghost locked!

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:41.190
Why can they move?!

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:45.200
I found the twelfth perp!

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:48.310
They're the host for the packaged virus.

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:49.660
Destroy their cyberbrain!

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:54.160
It's been a while since I got permission to kill.

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:26.750
Mr. Prime Minister, wait!

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:42.540
My ear!

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:44.960
That was a flesh part!

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:46.210
I'll kill that bastard!

00:22:57.130 --> 00:22:58.860
This is horrible...

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:06.290
A false cyberbrain...

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:10.300
This is just a remote-control doll with no Ghost!

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:11.490
Where's the twelfth perp?

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:14.320
I lost track. I'm searching now.

00:23:16.380 --> 00:23:18.710
A governmental state of emergency alert?

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:22.060
Secret talks at Yagasaki Hotel?

00:23:22.060 --> 00:23:23.510
Bombing?

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:25.840
What the hell are you talking about?! Who died?!

00:23:59.930 --> 00:24:03.640
The first assassination of a sitting 
Prime Minister in our nation's history

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:08.270
happened while Japanese soldiers occupied an East Asian Federation embassy.

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:10.260
The relationship between these events is unknown,

00:24:10.710 --> 00:24:14.920
but authorities requested an analysis 
of the Ministry faction's military Nets

00:24:14.920 --> 00:24:19.140
from Vice-Minister Kitahara Youko in her 
interim role due to the Minister's resignation.

00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:20.470
The administration is expected to force the downgrade to Defense Agency,

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:23.100
increasing the bad feeling between government and military groups.

00:24:48.130 --> 00:24:50.100
"Which of us is disposable..."

00:24:52.570 --> 00:24:54.750
Did someone use you and throw you away?

00:24:59.260 --> 00:25:04.110
I'll find them and put them on the slab next to you, Kurutsu.

00:25:05.370 --> 00:25:09.440
The PM's talks were with Ambassador Wong from the Far East trade embassy.

00:25:09.440 --> 00:25:13.700
Investigate the simultaneous embassy occupation without making any assumptions.

00:25:13.700 --> 00:25:14.480
Yes, sir!

00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:17.020
Find out what's been going on at the PM's residence.

00:25:17.020 --> 00:25:20.290
Put surveillance on anyone who makes noise about their immunity to arrest.

00:25:20.290 --> 00:25:21.370
Yes, sir.

00:25:35.240 --> 00:25:40.640
We should have stopped this from happening somehow!

00:25:43.240 --> 00:25:44.910
All patched up?

00:25:44.910 --> 00:25:47.600
Amazing what having a budget will do for maintenance.

00:25:48.250 --> 00:25:52.070
Who knows what'll happen with the budget now that the PM's dead, though.

00:25:52.070 --> 00:25:54.280
Give me two hours to fine-tune.

00:25:54.280 --> 00:25:57.030
I'm gonna blow the brains out of whoever shot me!

00:25:57.030 --> 00:26:00.200
You go after the one with the Major's body, Saito.

00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:01.910
You're the only one who saw her.

00:26:01.910 --> 00:26:02.990
I'll do both!

00:26:03.830 --> 00:26:05.460
So what now, Major?

00:26:06.180 --> 00:26:09.170
Paz, you're on the embassy. Borma, you're on the bomb site.

00:26:09.170 --> 00:26:11.740
Figure out whether this was an operation on two fronts.

00:26:11.740 --> 00:26:14.130
What about Kurutsu and company's cyberbrains?

00:26:14.130 --> 00:26:16.210
They're too damaged for me to read.

00:26:16.210 --> 00:26:18.640
I'll investigate her death and the virus.

00:26:19.200 --> 00:26:22.760
Let's say the chick with your body model unleashed the virus.

00:26:22.760 --> 00:26:23.930
Can I kill her?

00:26:23.930 --> 00:26:26.300
Do corpses give us info on the ringleader?

00:26:26.300 --> 00:26:28.010
Quit the kill shot habit, idiot.

00:26:29.460 --> 00:26:32.230
Are the rookie and I goin' after the perps, then?

00:26:32.230 --> 00:26:35.080
They oughta be halfway around the world by now.

00:26:35.080 --> 00:26:40.490
Nah, if their goal is to mess with domestic affairs, they'll have operatives in our government who can't move right away.

00:26:40.490 --> 00:26:46.220
In which case, there's a third party who used these guys and then iced them.

00:26:46.220 --> 00:26:49.190
I'll pray they're foreigners.

00:26:49.190 --> 00:26:50.790
I'm sick of killing my countrymen.

00:26:51.440 --> 00:26:53.310
Do background checks on everyone.

00:26:53.310 --> 00:26:55.920
Don't get tripped up by petty spy battles.

00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:01.830
Special Adviser Fujimoto...

00:27:09.020 --> 00:27:11.730
I came for the DNA testing on his body.

00:27:12.240 --> 00:27:15.590
He's not recognizable anymore, after all...

00:27:16.450 --> 00:27:18.700
I promise to find the culprit.

00:27:19.470 --> 00:27:24.620
My mind is so mixed up that when they question me,
 I can't even remember yesterday.

00:27:24.620 --> 00:27:26.980
Or what Father and I last talked about...

00:27:27.980 --> 00:27:31.030
I've experienced that, on the battlefield.

00:27:31.840 --> 00:27:34.090
Did your memories come back?

00:27:35.380 --> 00:27:36.880
All of them.

00:27:36.880 --> 00:27:38.520
I'll never forget again.

00:27:44.340 --> 00:27:48.750
Right before he died, he issued some kind of directive to me.

00:27:49.720 --> 00:27:52.340
But someone jammed the signal.

00:27:57.030 --> 00:27:58.100
Please...

00:27:58.100 --> 00:28:02.950
I want you to tell me his last message for me.

00:28:06.940 --> 00:28:08.590
Oh, and...

00:28:10.020 --> 00:28:12.630
Could we have dinner sometime?

00:28:12.630 --> 00:28:13.640
Pardon?

00:28:13.640 --> 00:28:16.340
I'd like to talk to you again, if that's all right.

00:28:18.070 --> 00:28:20.800
There aren't many restaurants I can go to.

00:28:30.230 --> 00:28:32.200
Ishikawa, I assume you heard.

00:28:32.200 --> 00:28:33.920
Yep. I'll find evidence.

00:28:44.200 --> 00:28:46.020
Want me to keep tabs on him, too?

00:28:46.020 --> 00:28:49.540
Get the perps' Net and don't do anything uncalled-for.

00:28:49.540 --> 00:28:53.600
Who tries to pick up women the day after his dad dies?

00:28:53.600 --> 00:28:55.240
Not to mention the Major!

00:28:55.240 --> 00:28:57.570
They probably hit it off from the start.

00:28:57.570 --> 00:29:01.700
Rich third-generation politicians don't meet her type every day.

00:29:01.700 --> 00:29:04.090
Now let's get to work, old-timer.

00:29:04.090 --> 00:29:05.680
Can't waste our new authority.

00:29:19.100 --> 00:29:21.590
It's been 900 hours since I last saw someone move.

00:29:22.570 --> 00:29:28.020
I heard about Unit 501 being privatized, but I didn't realize it would become an automated factory.

00:29:28.020 --> 00:29:30.720
Everyone went to work for Harimadara.

00:29:30.720 --> 00:29:32.050
What did you want?

00:29:32.050 --> 00:29:33.580
A factory tour?

00:29:34.300 --> 00:29:36.510
Why was Kurutsu at that meeting?

00:29:37.260 --> 00:29:38.960
For profit and survival.

00:29:39.420 --> 00:29:44.640
Ambassador Wong and the PM were working on an agreement to avoid a prosthetics development dead end.

00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:49.660
To keep production lines going by deliberately delaying technological improvements.

00:29:49.660 --> 00:29:54.750
Doesn't the government give research grants so that development won't dead-end?

00:29:54.750 --> 00:29:55.720
It's the opposite.

00:29:55.720 --> 00:29:59.900
Most of the existing prosthetics will be impossible to upgrade within the next generation.

00:30:00.720 --> 00:30:03.860
Others weren't full cyborgs from birth like you.

00:30:05.030 --> 00:30:07.890
You were developed on the premise of further growth,

00:30:07.890 --> 00:30:10.830
thanks to the keen insight of your designer, Dr. Kusanagi.

00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:14.390
So you're making parts here?

00:30:14.390 --> 00:30:16.790
Yes, to keep us alive.

00:30:16.790 --> 00:30:20.120
Technology conservation keeps vested interests going,

00:30:20.120 --> 00:30:23.630
while a technological revolution means control of an enormous market share.

00:30:23.630 --> 00:30:27.760
Kurutsu bet on the former, 
and was annihilated by the latter's system.

00:30:29.070 --> 00:30:34.590
That makes a strong motive for the perp to kill the ambassador and the PM in the same hit.

00:30:36.140 --> 00:30:37.710
Thanks for telling me.

00:30:38.740 --> 00:30:40.930
You should say hello to your parents.

00:30:40.930 --> 00:30:42.230
Another time.

00:30:42.230 --> 00:30:44.070
Come whenever you like.

00:30:44.070 --> 00:30:48.210
Much like us, they're not going anywhere.

00:30:51.750 --> 00:30:55.570
Sawada Kouichi, former Army armored division signal man.

00:30:55.570 --> 00:30:58.140
Would a military Net admin really hole up here?

00:30:58.140 --> 00:31:02.020
If the access logs left in the perps' cyberbrains are right, he did.

00:31:07.250 --> 00:31:08.580
Logicoma.

00:31:08.580 --> 00:31:10.710
I see one person's heat signature.

00:31:11.580 --> 00:31:13.370
And nobody's dead?

00:31:13.370 --> 00:31:15.420
My investigation doesn't go that far.

00:31:15.420 --> 00:31:17.580
Dead men tell no tales.

00:31:17.580 --> 00:31:20.710
He'd better be alive, or we're back where we started.

00:31:38.180 --> 00:31:39.710
You're a dangerous guest.

00:31:42.260 --> 00:31:43.670
Learn to shut your door.

00:31:47.380 --> 00:31:50.270
I thought someone might come to speak with me.

00:31:50.270 --> 00:31:51.840
Did you need something?

00:31:51.840 --> 00:31:53.740
Sawada Kouichi, I presume?

00:31:53.740 --> 00:31:54.890
We're part of a special squad.

00:31:54.890 --> 00:31:57.400
We'd like to ask you a few questions 
about the Prime Minister's assassination.

00:32:02.230 --> 00:32:03.650
What's that data?

00:32:03.650 --> 00:32:05.760
Soldiers' last words.

00:32:05.760 --> 00:32:10.110
They have no money to pass down, 
so they only send their dying messages.

00:32:11.070 --> 00:32:13.490
They automatically send to me after they kill themselves.

00:32:13.490 --> 00:32:19.450
Since they have no families, they choose me, 
an admin they've never even met.

00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:22.960
I wish they'd at least come talk to me...

00:32:22.960 --> 00:32:25.550
Is someone dead?

00:32:25.550 --> 00:32:27.570
Somewhere out there, yeah.

00:32:28.540 --> 00:32:29.960
You stand by until we get back.

00:32:29.960 --> 00:32:31.390
Okay!

00:32:32.860 --> 00:32:35.240
Get any transmissions that hinted at the Prime Minister's assassination?

00:32:35.240 --> 00:32:36.620
Not once.

00:32:36.620 --> 00:32:39.930
I do have the occupiers' testaments, though.

00:32:42.230 --> 00:32:43.980
Are there any you've lost contact with?

00:32:43.980 --> 00:32:45.320
Plenty.

00:32:45.320 --> 00:32:46.920
I'll forward you a list.

00:32:46.920 --> 00:32:49.000
Anybody you figure was in command?

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:50.110
Hmm,

00:32:50.930 --> 00:32:54.860
Army Colonel Nada Haruyoshi 
would have had the most clout.

00:32:54.860 --> 00:32:59.790
He was an informal adviser to Vice-Minister Kitahara, but he disappeared before the incident.

00:33:01.930 --> 00:33:04.370
You come talk to me first, too.

00:33:04.910 --> 00:33:06.610
Why me?

00:33:06.610 --> 00:33:09.630
Most suicides are full cyborgs.

00:33:09.630 --> 00:33:15.850
Cyberbrain standards change, meaning they can't use 
the newer prosthetics, so they fall apart while still alive.

00:33:21.350 --> 00:33:23.010
Like me.

00:33:24.450 --> 00:33:29.440
Without my role to play as a relay point, I would have killed myself, too.

00:33:33.070 --> 00:33:38.370
If the cyberbrain version you chose
 doesn't fit the tide of the times later,

00:33:39.540 --> 00:33:41.940
this is what prosthetization dooms you to.

00:33:46.580 --> 00:33:48.560
What did you do with the dead person?

00:33:48.560 --> 00:33:50.530
We couldn't do anything.

00:33:50.530 --> 00:33:54.920
If he can't be repaired, I recommend recovering his data!

00:33:54.920 --> 00:33:58.650
You can't recover his life or his Ghost if he's dead.

00:33:58.650 --> 00:34:00.990
What a badly designed unit.

00:34:00.990 --> 00:34:03.610
Have you ever died, Mr. Batou?

00:34:04.540 --> 00:34:08.190
I was supposed to, but I wound up a full cyborg instead.

00:34:08.720 --> 00:34:12.650
Are you working as one of the Major's parts so that you can die?

00:34:12.970 --> 00:34:14.220
Hey, now!

00:34:17.060 --> 00:34:20.500
A stud like me doesn't die too easily.

00:34:20.500 --> 00:34:21.580
Got it?

00:34:21.580 --> 00:34:25.980
Yes! Thank you for another valuable learning experience!

00:34:29.100 --> 00:34:31.920
Request it through Foreign Affairs.

00:34:32.460 --> 00:34:34.160
We're victims here.

00:34:34.160 --> 00:34:36.920
I won't allow you to "strip them of military affiliation."

00:34:37.640 --> 00:34:40.390
I want compensation from the government.

00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:45.580
That "victim" is trouble.

00:34:45.580 --> 00:34:48.550
That was Robert Lee, the Far East Trade Representative.

00:34:48.550 --> 00:34:50.810
He's also an infamous fixer.

00:34:50.810 --> 00:34:57.170
He almost got deported once at the Americans' request,
 but he weaseled his way out of it.

00:34:57.170 --> 00:35:00.980
He's got balls. For all he knows, he might be attacked again.

00:35:00.980 --> 00:35:03.740
He's probably got a lot of secrets he doesn't want exposed.

00:35:04.460 --> 00:35:08.770
Makes me want to know who arranged the PM's secret talks.

00:35:09.630 --> 00:35:12.230
And who leaked their location.

00:35:12.940 --> 00:35:16.880
Tell the Major I'm always open to a joint investigation.

00:35:35.900 --> 00:35:41.120
Standards are the national borders for corporations, just as they are for cyberbrains and prosthetics.

00:35:41.120 --> 00:35:46.240
No country relinquishes its borders just because 
national boundaries give rise to technology gaps.

00:35:46.240 --> 00:35:51.520
Lt. Col. Kurutsu and I were trying 
to find the way to the next epoch.

00:35:51.520 --> 00:35:56.470
Aren't you the ones who've profited from a system that transcends those borders,

00:35:56.470 --> 00:35:58.270
Deputy Director Amagata?

00:35:58.270 --> 00:35:59.880
That's no longer my title.

00:36:00.180 --> 00:36:02.000
Kurutsu told me the same thing—

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:06.390
that a day was bound to come when cyberbrain Nets would transcend even corporate borders.

00:36:07.300 --> 00:36:09.300
That's a long way off yet.

00:36:09.950 --> 00:36:14.560
If you feel you're in danger, 
I recommend our protection and monitoring.

00:36:15.360 --> 00:36:16.730
That's not necessary.

00:36:17.510 --> 00:36:20.860
Your former colleagues will protect my company.

00:36:28.980 --> 00:36:30.330
Major.

00:36:30.330 --> 00:36:31.580
You've got the info?

00:36:31.580 --> 00:36:37.220
No luck with the jamming yet, 
but I did find a data transfer from Kurutsu.

00:36:37.220 --> 00:36:40.790
It was an outside transmission, 
automatically sent one minute after the blast.

00:36:40.790 --> 00:36:44.010
And it wasn't some testament sent to the military Net, either.

00:36:44.010 --> 00:36:46.460
Give me the address. I'll go.

00:36:59.310 --> 00:37:03.530
So, all the members of the 501 are corporate employees now?

00:37:03.530 --> 00:37:05.860
Or are you research subjects?

00:37:05.860 --> 00:37:07.910
Please stay out of this, Kusanagi.

00:37:08.660 --> 00:37:10.120
Instructor Ibachi.

00:37:10.120 --> 00:37:12.720
We'll get justice for Kurutsu.

00:37:12.720 --> 00:37:15.260
Don't involve yourself any further.

00:37:15.260 --> 00:37:19.800
You're just an outcast who modifies her own parts, not even backed by a developmental organization.

00:37:20.540 --> 00:37:24.260
Get in our way, and I really will take you out this time.

00:37:36.220 --> 00:37:39.390
Keep tabs on everyone at Harimadara from the 501.

00:37:39.390 --> 00:37:40.960
Expect them to obstruct our investigation.

00:37:40.960 --> 00:37:42.120
Roger.

00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:44.240
They probably want to retaliate anyway.

00:37:45.020 --> 00:37:48.630
I found the plan for averting dead ends in some government docs.

00:37:48.630 --> 00:37:54.890
There's a security plan set up based on what happened 
over 20 years ago when they tried the same national policy.

00:37:54.890 --> 00:37:56.750
Security? What happened?

00:37:56.750 --> 00:37:59.150
A ton of people went missing.

00:37:59.150 --> 00:38:02.510
At the top of the list are a prosthetics researcher and his pregnant wife.

00:38:02.510 --> 00:38:06.340
They were last seen at the site of a chemical weapons explosion.

00:38:10.870 --> 00:38:14.130
Some organization is keeping their bodies for research...

00:38:15.170 --> 00:38:16.700
Are you listening?

00:38:19.610 --> 00:38:22.150
I'll have my AIs analyze the data.

00:38:22.150 --> 00:38:24.260
Find out the connection with these crimes.

00:38:33.590 --> 00:38:35.420
They tell me you're with another unit now.

00:38:39.140 --> 00:38:42.390
We have more non-military companies interviewing here recently.

00:38:42.390 --> 00:38:45.370
Now we foster a broader range of personnel.

00:38:45.370 --> 00:38:47.470
Are they good purchases for the corporations?

00:38:47.980 --> 00:38:50.430
The point is that we can promise these children a future.

00:38:54.560 --> 00:38:55.620
They're over there.

00:39:04.190 --> 00:39:06.920
Hello.

00:39:06.920 --> 00:39:08.260
What's your name?

00:39:08.910 --> 00:39:09.790
Chris.

00:39:10.460 --> 00:39:12.520
I'm Kusanagi Motoko.

00:39:12.520 --> 00:39:14.200
I used to live here.

00:39:15.180 --> 00:39:17.160
Do you feel nostalgic?

00:39:17.160 --> 00:39:20.550
Yes, I suppose it does bring back memories.

00:39:21.430 --> 00:39:22.940
Do you know Kurutsu?

00:39:22.940 --> 00:39:24.380
Everyone here does.

00:39:24.810 --> 00:39:27.600
She was going to build a future for us.

00:39:27.600 --> 00:39:29.380
But she died.

00:39:30.660 --> 00:39:32.840
May I listen to her message?

00:39:32.840 --> 00:39:33.300
Yes.

00:39:43.970 --> 00:39:49.950
If you are watching this, it means I'm no longer of this world.

00:39:51.160 --> 00:39:57.110
Check your individual Nets for the rights, assets, and duties I've assigned you.

00:39:58.210 --> 00:40:00.180
I'm sure you're worried, but there is a future.

00:40:00.900 --> 00:40:04.680
If you believe in the Third World, we'll meet again one day.

00:40:06.540 --> 00:40:07.870
"Third World"?

00:40:09.810 --> 00:40:12.590
A world not of people or things, but of data.

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:17.800
Do you believe that there's someplace we can go

00:40:17.800 --> 00:40:21.210
even if we become unable to swap prosthetics and we can't go on living?

00:40:23.490 --> 00:40:25.050
That's not something I know.

00:40:25.940 --> 00:40:27.430
Is this the only message?

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:28.730
Yes.

00:40:31.180 --> 00:40:32.200
Will we meet again?

00:40:35.350 --> 00:40:37.860
Good idea. Let's.

00:40:47.760 --> 00:40:49.370
Why meet up to talk?

00:40:49.370 --> 00:40:52.000
Are you implying my cyber lobby is bugged?

00:40:52.000 --> 00:40:57.220
No, it's just... It's important to talk over a meal sometimes instead of just doing it via cyberbrain, you know?

00:40:57.220 --> 00:40:59.120
What are you talking about?

00:40:59.120 --> 00:41:04.030
You're the one who chose to bring this flesh guy into our unified-spec team.

00:41:10.970 --> 00:41:16.020
Our rookie's afraid you might secretly be a robot.

00:41:16.020 --> 00:41:17.740
I didn't go that far!

00:41:17.740 --> 00:41:19.790
I just want to deepen our understanding and trust—

00:41:19.790 --> 00:41:21.780
He says this is a terrible working environment:

00:41:21.780 --> 00:41:25.170
No vacation, no fun, and no cherry blossom viewing even though it's spring.

00:41:25.170 --> 00:41:26.380
I didn't say that!

00:41:38.620 --> 00:41:40.180
So, about the Ministry faction...

00:41:40.870 --> 00:41:46.720
The eleven hostage-takers, plus Colonel Nada and seven MIAs, all left the same testament.

00:41:47.390 --> 00:41:52.150
Meaning they're all lying low somewhere, and they're likely to strike again.

00:41:52.560 --> 00:41:56.110
Colonel Nada's testament has an extra line, and it's a weird one.

00:41:56.110 --> 00:41:59.490
He said he'd "received a gift from the Third World."

00:42:00.080 --> 00:42:04.430
Doesn't that mean he got the virus from the broker?

00:42:04.430 --> 00:42:06.360
No... It's weird.

00:42:12.880 --> 00:42:15.760
"Third World"? Is this some occult thing?

00:42:15.760 --> 00:42:20.220
Find out if anyone at the Ministry of Defense or affiliated companies uses that phrase.

00:42:20.220 --> 00:42:22.660
Hire some more people, dammit.

00:42:22.660 --> 00:42:24.600
I will if I find optimal parts.

00:42:24.600 --> 00:42:26.470
Calling us parts again?

00:42:26.470 --> 00:42:27.730
Got a problem?

00:42:27.730 --> 00:42:32.500
The rookie says you're a crappy leader who talks about people like things.

00:42:33.150 --> 00:42:35.200
Seriously, I didn't go that far!

00:42:35.200 --> 00:42:36.650
Report for ya, Major.

00:42:36.650 --> 00:42:41.520
From the confiscated rifle and what I've seen at the crime scene, it was an RMC.

00:42:41.520 --> 00:42:44.120
They used a remotely controlled machine gun,
 not a human sniper.

00:42:44.120 --> 00:42:48.190
Someone did the shot, the virus, 
and remote-controlled a body at the same time?

00:42:48.190 --> 00:42:51.090
That's not the Major's body model—that's the Major!

00:42:51.490 --> 00:42:53.890
Just makes me wanna kill her more.

00:42:53.890 --> 00:42:58.010
Also, I keep sensing someone watching me.

00:42:58.010 --> 00:42:59.470
What a coincidence—

00:43:00.660 --> 00:43:01.930
so do I.

00:43:07.210 --> 00:43:08.990
Me, too, actually.

00:43:08.990 --> 00:43:10.610
Ape-Face from Section 9?

00:43:10.610 --> 00:43:12.560
No, this feels different.

00:43:12.560 --> 00:43:15.450
I found something that's probably related.

00:43:15.450 --> 00:43:18.530
Come to my lobby, and I'll show you something interesting.

00:43:21.750 --> 00:43:23.450
What'd you wanna show us?

00:43:23.450 --> 00:43:28.320
I used a forensic search to reproduce the movements of objects caught in the blast.

00:43:46.600 --> 00:43:51.230
This is pyro reverse measurement—
it's like replaying the explosion backwards.

00:43:51.700 --> 00:43:53.190
Pretty amazing.

00:44:08.910 --> 00:44:12.040
The case with the bomb in it used fingerprint recognition.

00:44:12.040 --> 00:44:13.880
Only the Prime Minister or his aides could open it.

00:44:19.760 --> 00:44:21.300
A surveillance cam?

00:44:21.300 --> 00:44:23.940
It's military, but it's got a limited range of transmission.

00:44:23.940 --> 00:44:26.220
I did random testing with some white noise.

00:44:26.700 --> 00:44:30.190
This is cheap encryption by AI.

00:44:30.190 --> 00:44:32.190
Okay, I'm connected to our Peeping Tom's Net.

00:44:39.530 --> 00:44:41.270
I want your name and outfit!

00:44:41.270 --> 00:44:44.490
And FYI, my assassin's itching to kill someone.

00:44:57.300 --> 00:44:59.650
I'm with the Treaty Review Department, Section D!

00:44:59.650 --> 00:45:00.670
Contact them!

00:45:01.780 --> 00:45:03.680
He's on loan to Foreign Affairs from Public Security.

00:45:06.100 --> 00:45:09.050
They're involved with the PM's secret talks?

00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:28.200
I'm Akiyama, Treaty Review Department section leader.

00:45:28.490 --> 00:45:30.160
Give me the short and sweet explanation.

00:45:31.240 --> 00:45:33.620
We captured her on camera a month ago.

00:45:33.980 --> 00:45:40.550
Fire-Starter, the supposedly impossible trifecta of brainwashing, Ghost infiltration, and false memories...

00:45:40.550 --> 00:45:42.540
She's the seller.

00:45:42.540 --> 00:45:45.090
A crazy bitch who goes by the same name as the virus.

00:45:45.740 --> 00:45:49.160
You approached her to get the virus, and you fell into her trap.

00:45:49.160 --> 00:45:52.140
So you put tabs on me, since we have the same body.

00:45:52.140 --> 00:45:53.310
You're a fool.

00:45:53.310 --> 00:45:58.020
You're a super-wizard-class hacker. I'd be stupid not to suspect you.

00:46:03.070 --> 00:46:05.780
It was two officers that she manipulated.

00:46:05.780 --> 00:46:06.820
Officers?

00:46:06.820 --> 00:46:09.950
People who helped implement the PM's established policies.

00:46:09.950 --> 00:46:12.730
One of them was Colonel Nada Haruyoshi.

00:46:12.730 --> 00:46:14.620
The one who went missing before the incident?

00:46:14.620 --> 00:46:19.360
His job was to isolate the radical elements within the Ministry faction.

00:46:19.360 --> 00:46:23.300
And then he up and pulled the trigger on a two-pronged terrorist attack!

00:46:23.300 --> 00:46:25.600
It's like he had a personality transplant.

00:46:25.600 --> 00:46:27.260
He was infected by the virus.

00:46:28.130 --> 00:46:30.100
Would the broker go that far, though?

00:46:30.440 --> 00:46:34.090
Enemies of the PM must have bought the virus at auction.

00:46:34.090 --> 00:46:38.100
I want to find out who they were,
 and get hold of them <i>and</i> the broker.

00:46:38.770 --> 00:46:40.440
Who was the other officer?

00:46:44.110 --> 00:46:47.380
Kitahara Youko, Vice-Minister of Defense.

00:46:51.270 --> 00:46:52.580
Wh-What's the meaning of this?!

00:46:57.340 --> 00:46:58.500
Don't move!

00:46:58.500 --> 00:47:00.210
You protocol-ignoring scumbags!

00:47:00.670 --> 00:47:02.920
You're under arrest for unlawful investigation!

00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:04.190
Knock it off.

00:47:07.840 --> 00:47:10.800
I... never expected this...

00:47:11.810 --> 00:47:13.510
Let's hear your story.

00:47:17.500 --> 00:47:21.440
She was infected by Nada, and she induced the Ministry faction's flare-up.

00:47:22.020 --> 00:47:26.740
She manipulated public opinion for the "Agency" downgrade, laying off several thousand troops in the restructuring.

00:47:27.400 --> 00:47:30.080
Was she involved in the PM's assassination?

00:47:30.080 --> 00:47:31.620
Not that we've discovered.

00:47:32.260 --> 00:47:38.080
So a Foreign Affairs squad and the backbone of the MoD got used in a plot to assassinate the PM.

00:47:38.080 --> 00:47:40.670
The virus itself hasn't been found.

00:47:40.670 --> 00:47:43.000
If it's all this woman's scheme...

00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:46.120
I saw this from the cyberbrain infringement stage.

00:47:46.120 --> 00:47:47.710
I'm aware that I'm a victim.

00:47:48.420 --> 00:47:51.560
Who orchestrated this to make this look like my set-up?

00:47:51.560 --> 00:47:52.690
Excuse me?!

00:47:52.690 --> 00:47:54.550
He's not Section 9, is he?

00:47:55.090 --> 00:47:57.720
That's Kuwahara, head of intelligence's strategy office.

00:47:57.720 --> 00:48:00.270
He's after the broker who could be your twin.

00:48:00.270 --> 00:48:01.300
Aramaki!

00:48:01.300 --> 00:48:06.020
So it was the intelligence bureau that outbid the treaties bureau for the virus?

00:48:06.860 --> 00:48:09.080
I've got nothing to do with the treaties bureau.

00:48:09.080 --> 00:48:13.700
The purchase was a ruse to arrest the broker, and she got away from us before we could secure the virus.

00:48:13.700 --> 00:48:16.160
I'll pretend I believe that.

00:48:16.800 --> 00:48:20.190
Right now we need everyone working together on this.

00:48:20.190 --> 00:48:22.470
Quit being stubborn and team up with us, Major.

00:48:25.900 --> 00:48:30.990
An organization that locks up witnesses to protect itself deserves to be punished along with the perps.

00:48:30.990 --> 00:48:33.480
You're just some upstart rogue squad!

00:48:33.480 --> 00:48:36.200
I'll call you when we take her down,

00:48:36.200 --> 00:48:38.530
so you can have something to do afterward.

00:48:48.670 --> 00:48:53.410
That squad has traced things back to Kitahara, Fire-Starter.

00:48:53.940 --> 00:48:57.370
They're nuisances. Can't you take them over with your virus?

00:48:57.370 --> 00:48:59.400
No need to panic.

00:48:59.400 --> 00:49:01.830
Intelligence and the Treaty Review Department are both under my thumb,

00:49:02.330 --> 00:49:05.790
and the truth is the biggest trap, the biggest tragedy, of all.

00:49:05.790 --> 00:49:10.140
Simply taking advantage of people's patriotism isn't a foolproof plan.

00:49:10.140 --> 00:49:13.260
We should eliminate any possibility of them tracing this back to us.

00:49:13.710 --> 00:49:15.970
That will cost you.

00:49:37.220 --> 00:49:39.040
Kusanagi Motoko...

00:49:39.040 --> 00:49:41.590
Now, when shall I steal your name?

00:49:46.020 --> 00:49:51.200
Prime Minister Fujimoto definitely issued some sort of directive.

00:49:51.200 --> 00:49:56.620
And our only related lead is that
 Vice-Minister Kitahara remembers

00:49:56.620 --> 00:49:59.970
a ghost ship of unknown origin off the coast of Niihama.

00:49:59.970 --> 00:50:02.490
Nada's hideout...

00:50:02.490 --> 00:50:04.860
And yet intelligence isn't making a move.

00:50:04.860 --> 00:50:08.440
If Nada's infected like the treaties bureau says...

00:50:09.140 --> 00:50:11.550
Odds are ten to one it's a trap.

00:50:12.810 --> 00:50:16.820
The ship's likely location is near a cluster of undersea cables.

00:50:16.820 --> 00:50:18.410
Could be a spy vessel.

00:50:18.990 --> 00:50:22.910
This is all the info we have, thanks to intelligence stealing Kitahara from us.

00:50:22.910 --> 00:50:23.870
Now what?

00:50:23.870 --> 00:50:25.830
We find out the rest by taking over the ship.

00:50:29.360 --> 00:50:31.340
You just love storming enemy positions, don't you?

00:50:31.340 --> 00:50:33.550
Quit the squad if you've got doubts.

00:50:34.620 --> 00:50:36.960
Everything ties back to the PM.

00:50:36.960 --> 00:50:40.300
Will you get to the truth, or back out now?

00:50:41.020 --> 00:50:43.200
Let your Ghosts decide.

00:51:31.530 --> 00:51:35.970
There's a new home where you're headed, yeah?

00:51:35.970 --> 00:51:40.620
Not a bloody battlefield or a tight corner to die in.

00:51:44.620 --> 00:51:49.630
I plan to get us a position that suits us, if nothing else.

00:52:00.900 --> 00:52:03.410
Just stand by. We don't know what we're facing.

00:52:04.600 --> 00:52:07.330
"An offensive unit with top priority..."

00:52:08.080 --> 00:52:13.420
Plenty have talked about it, but nobody's made it a reality...

00:52:13.420 --> 00:52:14.720
Until now.

00:52:21.580 --> 00:52:23.240
No sign of anyone on board.

00:52:42.130 --> 00:52:42.720
Incoming!

00:52:48.620 --> 00:52:50.410
They're pulling out the tanks from the get-go?!

00:52:52.140 --> 00:52:54.440
I knew I should've stayed home!

00:52:54.440 --> 00:52:55.510
Saito!

00:52:57.070 --> 00:52:59.030
I can't pick them up!

00:53:01.500 --> 00:53:02.600
Shit.

00:53:04.280 --> 00:53:06.990
That's type-2902 thermo-optical camouflage—

00:53:06.990 --> 00:53:08.950
Kyo-Re's newest release!

00:53:09.530 --> 00:53:13.260
How much capital would it take to get that for your tanks and your troops?

00:53:16.980 --> 00:53:18.710
I'm taking the ship. Cover me!

00:53:20.800 --> 00:53:22.630
How, exactly?!

00:53:23.870 --> 00:53:25.800
I'll show you how it's done, rookie.

00:53:40.740 --> 00:53:41.150
Go!

00:54:41.650 --> 00:54:43.050
Go, Major!

00:55:03.460 --> 00:55:05.810
I've reached the intermediate security server.

00:55:06.760 --> 00:55:08.660
I have eyes on the barrier's gate array.

00:55:10.820 --> 00:55:13.430
It's a variant on Army tactical defense barriers.

00:55:14.100 --> 00:55:16.740
Lots of entrances, but only one exit...

00:55:16.740 --> 00:55:18.670
This'll be a pain.

00:55:19.350 --> 00:55:21.080
Opening a tunnel.

00:55:21.080 --> 00:55:23.680
Shit, it's full of null data.

00:55:23.680 --> 00:55:25.230
They're giving me the slip!

00:55:25.230 --> 00:55:26.900
This fake looks familiar.

00:55:26.900 --> 00:55:28.620
The real data is on the other side of the nulls.

00:55:28.620 --> 00:55:30.430
I'll look for a way around.

00:55:30.430 --> 00:55:32.630
I don't want to wait. I'll just force it open.

00:55:43.160 --> 00:55:45.800
The broadcast van's active protection burned out!

00:55:45.800 --> 00:55:46.970
Close the connection!

00:55:46.970 --> 00:55:47.570
Too late!

00:56:04.700 --> 00:56:05.480
What?

00:56:08.340 --> 00:56:11.760
Jeez, how many hidden servers do you have?

00:56:11.760 --> 00:56:14.310
I don't storm a place unarmed.

00:56:14.310 --> 00:56:16.680
I've taken control. The info—

00:56:18.910 --> 00:56:20.530
What is this?

00:56:21.640 --> 00:56:24.290
Signals 2, 6, and 7 lost.

00:56:24.290 --> 00:56:26.640
Number and positioning of enemy troops unknown.

00:56:26.640 --> 00:56:29.070
They've taken our fire-control room!

00:56:52.020 --> 00:56:54.280
Okay, I've got him.

00:56:58.390 --> 00:57:00.090
We're done here, too.

00:57:05.810 --> 00:57:06.710
Hit the deck!

00:57:11.740 --> 00:57:13.230
Another one?!

00:57:13.230 --> 00:57:14.790
Mr. Batou!

00:57:20.970 --> 00:57:21.910
Stop!

00:57:22.340 --> 00:57:24.600
When are you gonna get a cockpit?!

00:57:24.600 --> 00:57:26.380
The request is being processed!

00:57:27.810 --> 00:57:29.470
Military restructuring?

00:57:29.470 --> 00:57:31.090
Why my team?

00:57:31.840 --> 00:57:33.360
Who the hell—

00:57:37.670 --> 00:57:39.600
So that's how it is?

00:57:43.100 --> 00:57:45.230
Get out of there now, Major!

00:57:46.300 --> 00:57:48.140
What's your status, Major?!

00:57:55.570 --> 00:57:57.840
Hey, what the hell's going on?!

00:57:57.840 --> 00:57:59.960
I know we took over the ship.

00:57:59.960 --> 00:58:03.110
Somebody's remote-controlling these from nearby.

00:58:04.760 --> 00:58:07.690
Saito! Find them and kill them!

00:58:08.330 --> 00:58:10.290
Give me more intel!

00:58:14.320 --> 00:58:15.260
That bitch!

00:58:18.340 --> 00:58:19.640
Oh, you're good.

00:58:19.640 --> 00:58:22.220
You can work for me when she's dead.

00:58:29.580 --> 00:58:30.930
Dammit.

00:58:30.930 --> 00:58:32.030
She got away, guys!

00:58:41.040 --> 00:58:43.440
Why isn't anyone shooting at us?

00:58:43.440 --> 00:58:45.580
Isn't their goal to recapture the ship?

00:58:46.780 --> 00:58:47.960
Everyone all right?

00:58:47.960 --> 00:58:48.710
Major?!

00:58:49.580 --> 00:58:50.590
What the—

00:58:50.880 --> 00:58:52.530
Did she use Ghost infiltration keys?

00:58:52.530 --> 00:58:54.460
She assembled us by force.

00:58:54.460 --> 00:58:57.050
There's no time, so I'll make this brief.

00:58:57.050 --> 00:59:01.070
I'm redoing the investigation with a new hypothesis in mind.

00:59:01.070 --> 00:59:03.380
There's no need for us all to bear the risk.

00:59:04.310 --> 00:59:05.320
Major?

00:59:05.320 --> 00:59:07.220
It's not her. Just projected data.

00:59:07.220 --> 00:59:10.060
I just declared this squad disbanded.

00:59:11.090 --> 00:59:12.040
Say what?!

00:59:12.040 --> 00:59:14.880
I'll leave recommendation letters with Chief Aramaki.

00:59:14.880 --> 00:59:17.150
Choose for yourselves where you want to transfer to.

00:59:18.150 --> 00:59:20.470
You're top-notch parts.

00:59:21.170 --> 00:59:26.540
When you're all together,
 you perform better than I could alone.

00:59:30.020 --> 00:59:31.060
That's all.

00:59:31.060 --> 00:59:32.950
Obey your Ghosts.

00:59:36.100 --> 00:59:37.880
Her lobby's been shut down.

00:59:37.880 --> 00:59:40.260
She purged herself.

00:59:40.940 --> 00:59:43.430
She might've just cut us off.

00:59:43.430 --> 00:59:46.150
It's messed up either way.

00:59:53.860 --> 00:59:55.730
My ghost lock ain't working!

01:00:07.980 --> 01:00:10.110
A remote-controlled body...

01:00:33.510 --> 01:00:35.590
Was Colonel Nada captured?

01:00:37.910 --> 01:00:40.630
You're upset that the hearing was indefinitely postponed?

01:00:42.050 --> 01:00:45.580
I don't even know what the truth is myself!

01:00:45.960 --> 01:00:47.240
I'm not upset.

01:01:30.180 --> 01:01:33.970
Send the repair bill to the Ministry of Commerce or the Far East trade embassy.

01:01:33.970 --> 01:01:36.040
I'm borrowing another car.

01:01:37.110 --> 01:01:39.160
"Fire-Starter"...

01:01:39.160 --> 01:01:42.180
Was that just the virus's code name during development,

01:01:42.180 --> 01:01:44.400
or is it your own name?

01:01:45.040 --> 01:01:46.580
Is there a difference?

01:01:48.050 --> 01:01:51.000
I abandoned the spy vessel, just like you asked.

01:01:51.000 --> 01:01:53.480
What more do you want?!

01:01:53.480 --> 01:01:56.760
We don't know whether Kusanagi is dead or alive.

01:01:56.760 --> 01:01:58.870
Search your Net for her.

01:02:00.100 --> 01:02:01.470
Cooperate...

01:02:02.490 --> 01:02:05.870
Or else the biggest scandal since the war is going public.

01:02:17.670 --> 01:02:21.670
Section 9 Office

01:02:17.670 --> 01:02:21.670
Section 9 Office

01:02:20.830 --> 01:02:26.120
Vice-Minister Kitahara was assassinated, and Colonel Nada is still status unknown.

01:02:26.120 --> 01:02:31.260
That makes your case hard to corroborate, 
and you've also lost your investigative privileges.

01:02:31.910 --> 01:02:35.100
But you can stay on the investigation if you do it as members of Section 9.

01:02:36.430 --> 01:02:37.730
Not interested.

01:02:39.500 --> 01:02:41.100
I'm outta here.

01:02:40.340 --> 01:02:41.100
Hey, wait—

01:02:41.100 --> 01:02:43.530
You guys are fine with this?!

01:02:50.530 --> 01:02:52.270
Where do you want to restart from?

01:02:53.890 --> 01:02:56.020
If the boat didn't give us anything,

01:02:56.020 --> 01:02:59.170
I'd look into anybody involved who refuses to testify.

01:02:59.170 --> 01:03:01.920
You mean Robert Lee, the Far East trade rep.

01:03:02.580 --> 01:03:04.130
He's a formidable opponent.

01:03:04.130 --> 01:03:06.010
Use Section 9's Net.

01:03:06.010 --> 01:03:06.950
Yes, sir!

01:03:12.400 --> 01:03:15.530
What you cultivated is starting to thrive.

01:03:15.530 --> 01:03:18.540
I won't let it be cut down, Major.

01:03:26.640 --> 01:03:28.450
There was this intel...

01:03:29.060 --> 01:03:33.910
Two developers, a married couple, went MIA during the old project to avert dead-ending.

01:03:34.260 --> 01:03:35.970
I just did some digging.

01:03:35.970 --> 01:03:39.870
Their bodies are being kept by 
Unit 501 for research purposes.

01:03:41.490 --> 01:03:44.650
You better not tell me the wife was pregnant.

01:03:44.650 --> 01:03:46.070
What are you talking about?

01:03:48.500 --> 01:03:51.340
Someone who's been a full cyborg since birth.

01:03:52.460 --> 01:03:53.910
They're the Major's parents?

01:03:54.430 --> 01:03:56.760
I can't be sure.

01:03:56.760 --> 01:03:59.830
The bodies are so contaminated they can't even be ID'd.

01:04:01.910 --> 01:04:06.520
She was born without a body of her own, and raised as Army equipment.

01:04:07.210 --> 01:04:09.110
It's not that she has nothing to lose...

01:04:09.820 --> 01:04:12.640
It's that she never had anything she could lose.

01:04:14.380 --> 01:04:18.490
Until the war ended and she went independent, you're saying?

01:04:19.780 --> 01:04:23.870
So your take is that those vics who might be her parents are the reason she's gone rogue?

01:04:24.530 --> 01:04:26.140
This is the Major.

01:04:26.140 --> 01:04:28.980
They're probably secondary to something bigger she's after.

01:04:30.170 --> 01:04:35.300
This is just me speculating, but I think
 she saw something real bad on that ship.

01:04:35.300 --> 01:04:38.400
Bad enough to make her purge all of us.

01:04:39.680 --> 01:04:42.800
If you're implying she wants to protect us, that's a laugh.

01:04:42.800 --> 01:04:44.830
She calls us "parts"!

01:04:45.560 --> 01:04:49.190
She talks like we're things, 
but she doesn't treat us like things.

01:04:49.760 --> 01:04:52.630
Full cyborgs are parts anyway, really.

01:04:53.340 --> 01:04:58.160
Gotta join some organization who'll do your maintenance, or fall apart while you're still alive.

01:05:11.060 --> 01:05:12.340
Where are you going?

01:05:14.120 --> 01:05:16.430
I'm not the type to obey my Ghost.

01:05:17.920 --> 01:05:20.280
What I can see with my own eyes is all there is.

01:05:24.330 --> 01:05:28.200
One ship, two tanks, and seven infantrymen.

01:05:28.890 --> 01:05:31.240
That was one expensive trap.

01:06:00.250 --> 01:06:02.040
What were they looking at?

01:06:17.100 --> 01:06:18.680
I came to talk.

01:06:25.380 --> 01:06:28.080
Sorry for asking you here out of the blue.

01:06:28.080 --> 01:06:30.710
I hear you want to work for us again.

01:06:30.710 --> 01:06:34.570
If you give me intel on Major Kusanagi, I'll consider it.

01:06:37.150 --> 01:06:39.060
You're the one doing the talking.

01:06:42.740 --> 01:06:46.950
My role as a relay point... is...

01:06:47.560 --> 01:06:51.170
Sawada Kouichi, formerly of the Army's armored division.

01:06:51.170 --> 01:06:56.830
That name matches one of the Ministry loyalists who died yesterday on a spy ship of unknown affiliation.

01:06:57.520 --> 01:06:58.690
I...

01:07:02.900 --> 01:07:05.780
You've been implanted with false memories...

01:07:05.780 --> 01:07:07.510
Colonel Nada Haruyoshi.

