01:07:24.260 --> 01:07:29.190
Damn you, Ishikawa, do you think you can get away with making enemies of your old unit?!

01:07:30.310 --> 01:07:34.020
This is filled with micromachines that increase pain sensitivity 7,000-fold.

01:07:34.020 --> 01:07:36.640
It takes them five minutes to reach your cyberbrain.

01:07:36.640 --> 01:07:38.650
It ain't the kind of thing you can withstand.

01:07:38.650 --> 01:07:39.800
Stop!

01:07:41.320 --> 01:07:42.870
Stop!

01:08:05.630 --> 01:08:06.640
From the inside?!

01:08:31.570 --> 01:08:32.430
Get in!

01:08:37.380 --> 01:08:42.640
The East Asian Federation bigwigs and the cyborg with the Major's model have been together from the beginning.

01:08:42.640 --> 01:08:45.630
That rules out a terror strike on two fronts.

01:08:45.630 --> 01:08:47.640
Why were you at the embassy?

01:08:48.080 --> 01:08:51.230
I managed to play back a scrap of the data

01:08:51.930 --> 01:08:54.640
from that oversized e-paper at the bomb site.

01:08:57.140 --> 01:08:59.190
A 3D map of the embassy?

01:08:59.620 --> 01:09:02.670
Then the point of the PM's secret talks was...

01:09:04.600 --> 01:09:09.240
The ship was being used for domestic espionage under a secret deal with the Americans.

01:09:09.830 --> 01:09:13.140
Forget a scandal—this is a national security issue!

01:09:13.140 --> 01:09:16.230
But you gave it up. Why go so far to set up the Major?

01:09:16.230 --> 01:09:17.500
Who's the Prime Minister's enemy?!

01:09:18.070 --> 01:09:22.860
The PM wanted to use the Defense Ministry faction to oust the rebels in the Ministry of Commerce.

01:09:23.820 --> 01:09:25.560
That's all I know!

01:09:25.560 --> 01:09:27.420
Please, give me the antidote!

01:09:37.160 --> 01:09:39.460
It's a vitamin injection, idiot.

01:09:54.890 --> 01:09:57.400
He's Colonel Nada?

01:09:57.400 --> 01:10:01.640
Maybe his sympathy for the rank and file spawned his false memories.

01:10:01.640 --> 01:10:07.010
You think the host's desire and guilt 
form the core of the false memories?

01:10:07.490 --> 01:10:11.500
And they left him alive as a card to play when they wanted to intimidate the government.

01:10:12.200 --> 01:10:14.080
Unbelievable.

01:10:15.740 --> 01:10:21.150
After the incident, Representative Lee took over a rare earth mine that had been under Wong's jurisdiction.

01:10:21.830 --> 01:10:25.270
They were outwardly cooperative, but they were competitors.

01:10:25.980 --> 01:10:28.920
This is all about war merchants trying to crush each other.

01:10:29.810 --> 01:10:34.580
The PM must've helped with the Ambassador's plan to kill the Representative.

01:10:35.220 --> 01:10:37.990
And the Representative counterattacked.

01:10:38.540 --> 01:10:42.380
Our broker provided both sides with the virus.

01:10:43.100 --> 01:10:45.220
Probably playing a double game.

01:10:45.220 --> 01:10:50.100
When you get down to it, this was a war between the PM and the Federation!

01:10:58.120 --> 01:10:59.100
Got it.

01:10:59.810 --> 01:11:02.170
Someone's ordered the Major's arrest.

01:11:03.350 --> 01:11:04.320
Where are you going?

01:11:06.580 --> 01:11:09.660
Even the Major decided to go this one alone.

01:11:09.660 --> 01:11:12.190
I know you guys won't act.

01:11:13.340 --> 01:11:15.200
Don't underestimate me.

01:11:15.200 --> 01:11:16.800
I'll leave the Major to you.

01:11:16.800 --> 01:11:18.150
Do not let her die.

01:11:40.060 --> 01:11:41.520
Major Kusanagi?

01:11:43.730 --> 01:11:47.090
Section 9 told me to call them if you showed up.

01:11:48.280 --> 01:11:50.320
You want to keep this secret even from them?

01:11:50.320 --> 01:11:53.490
That depends on you, Special Advisor Fujimoto.

01:12:26.580 --> 01:12:31.520
You carried the enemy's bomb to your father.

01:12:31.520 --> 01:12:32.900
Oh, God...

01:12:34.370 --> 01:12:39.430
One more thing. My squad's budget—
I couldn't trace some of it.

01:12:39.430 --> 01:12:41.150
Where did that money come from?

01:12:44.370 --> 01:12:46.390
I think it's a surplus...

01:12:47.830 --> 01:12:50.800
from privatizing a military wing...

01:12:51.650 --> 01:12:53.430
From breaking up a post called Unit 501.

01:12:54.480 --> 01:12:57.800
Please, put my memories back how they were!

01:12:58.510 --> 01:13:00.430
I can't bear these memories!

01:13:01.320 --> 01:13:03.500
I choose the truth.

01:13:04.190 --> 01:13:09.090
I don't want to exchange my memories for fabricated ones, 
no matter how much my heart might wish it.

01:13:09.650 --> 01:13:10.720
Never again.

01:13:30.380 --> 01:13:32.090
A remote-controlled body...

01:13:40.020 --> 01:13:41.010
Kurutsu!

01:14:10.840 --> 01:14:12.510
Show me to the server floor.

01:14:55.780 --> 01:14:58.860
A virus development Net... It's transmitting externally?!

01:15:14.820 --> 01:15:17.690
An attack barrier and a barrier maze.

01:15:17.690 --> 01:15:20.530
Clearly that info is something worth protecting to you two.

01:15:20.530 --> 01:15:23.480
Your brain associated us with our old bodies, I see.

01:15:23.480 --> 01:15:25.500
We're sorry, but we're going to restrain you.

01:15:26.120 --> 01:15:27.520
On Kurutsu's orders?

01:15:27.520 --> 01:15:29.530
No, it's our collective will.

01:15:29.530 --> 01:15:31.380
Kurutsu is only one part.

01:15:31.690 --> 01:15:33.380
Then she <i>is</i> alive.

01:15:35.660 --> 01:15:37.670
Please don't fight, Kusanagi.

01:15:37.670 --> 01:15:39.590
We don't want to see you killed.

01:16:19.010 --> 01:16:20.600
That's enough.

01:16:20.600 --> 01:16:22.470
Leave it be, Kusanagi.

01:16:29.380 --> 01:16:30.690
Outcast.

01:16:44.280 --> 01:16:45.620
Out of my way!

01:17:31.900 --> 01:17:35.000
You've reached your limit, Kusanagi.

01:17:53.490 --> 01:17:55.590
Major!

01:18:16.220 --> 01:18:17.460
Yo. Awake now?

01:18:18.090 --> 01:18:20.800
I cracked your secret lab to use it.

01:18:20.800 --> 01:18:21.670
No complaining.

01:18:22.380 --> 01:18:27.590
It ain't like you to lower your body's 
functionality with implanted weapons.

01:18:28.750 --> 01:18:29.970
Why did you come?

01:18:30.560 --> 01:18:32.870
How about you just be honest and say,

01:18:32.870 --> 01:18:39.200
"As your leader I couldn't order you to come with me, but as a human with a Ghost I wanted to give you the choice"?

01:18:39.200 --> 01:18:40.460
Run.

01:18:40.460 --> 01:18:42.360
Sure, once you're out of the maze.

01:18:42.720 --> 01:18:45.360
Until then, we're gonna do our own thing.

01:18:55.780 --> 01:18:57.370
I hope you can take responsibility for this!

01:18:57.700 --> 01:19:00.760
Don't worry. I'll use members of the unit.

01:19:00.760 --> 01:19:03.520
I'll have my subsidiaries give you soldiers.

01:19:03.520 --> 01:19:05.470
Go through as many as you like.

01:19:05.990 --> 01:19:08.430
You don't mind battlefield-level casualties?

01:19:08.940 --> 01:19:12.290
Not when a 500 billion dollar deal is on the line.

01:19:12.290 --> 01:19:16.390
Fools out to change the world are a minority group.

01:19:16.950 --> 01:19:20.940
Isn't getting rid of those fast what your "democracy" is all about?

01:19:38.380 --> 01:19:40.520
Don't resist, Kusanagi.

01:19:40.520 --> 01:19:42.840
We don't want to see your brain fried.

01:19:42.840 --> 01:19:46.450
My barrier isn't that cheap.

01:19:52.840 --> 01:19:54.900
To think you reverse-breached the barrier...

01:19:54.900 --> 01:19:56.520
There'll be no going back for any of us.

01:19:56.930 --> 01:20:01.480
Tell me the real Kurutsu's location and objective before that happens.

01:20:01.930 --> 01:20:03.630
We don't know her location.

01:20:03.630 --> 01:20:06.880
Her having multiple bodies was top-secret.

01:20:06.880 --> 01:20:11.450
Her objective is the same as ever: survive no matter who wins this.

01:20:12.290 --> 01:20:14.150
I assume you know this,

01:20:14.150 --> 01:20:18.460
but the East Asian Federation's goals are technological revolution through dead-ending and market monopoly.

01:20:19.930 --> 01:20:23.730
Some children aren't facing a dead end yet.

01:20:23.730 --> 01:20:25.920
You'd turn them into merchandise?!

01:20:26.390 --> 01:20:28.880
They are our successors, 
to whom we should leave everything.

01:20:29.260 --> 01:20:33.850
They will become next-generation models and make long-term upgrading a reality.

01:20:33.850 --> 01:20:36.680
And you'll make them repeat all this?

01:20:36.680 --> 01:20:38.510
Sell even their Ghosts?!

01:21:17.890 --> 01:21:18.720
Why, you...

01:21:50.750 --> 01:21:53.010
You were always free.

01:21:53.350 --> 01:21:55.520
Constantly trying to create a future.

01:21:55.520 --> 01:21:57.970
We envy you for that.

01:21:58.380 --> 01:22:00.550
You protected me?!

01:22:00.550 --> 01:22:03.140
Our brains are at their limit anyway.

01:22:03.790 --> 01:22:06.680
We'll shift to the Third World before they expire.

01:22:06.680 --> 01:22:09.650
Pray that we become part of the sea of data.

01:22:10.780 --> 01:22:14.450
Someday, someone may be born who accesses you.

01:22:41.910 --> 01:22:43.270
There!

01:23:19.180 --> 01:23:20.150
Saito!

01:23:20.150 --> 01:23:22.310
How dare that bastard screw with me?!

01:23:31.180 --> 01:23:32.780
Hey guys, everybody alive?

01:23:32.780 --> 01:23:34.980
We can't repair you if you die, you know!

01:23:35.450 --> 01:23:37.450
We studs don't die!

01:24:08.180 --> 01:24:09.660
Why are you just standing there?

01:24:09.660 --> 01:24:12.150
I'll replace you if you don't perform better.

01:24:13.880 --> 01:24:16.860
I was just about to show my stuff, you damn maniac.

01:24:44.290 --> 01:24:45.350
Major!

01:24:57.650 --> 01:25:00.630
You outcast scum!

01:25:21.260 --> 01:25:22.980
Major, are you all right?

01:25:49.040 --> 01:25:51.330
Normal prosthetics are the best, am I right?

01:25:52.050 --> 01:25:55.710
I told you to run, you thrill-seeking idiots.

01:25:56.440 --> 01:26:00.670
You're the kind of parts I won't be able to collect again!

01:26:02.340 --> 01:26:04.910
We've got an important job still undone.

01:26:13.450 --> 01:26:16.060
What good will arresting me do?

01:26:16.060 --> 01:26:19.770
The same game will just start up again after this administration dissolves.

01:26:20.080 --> 01:26:24.730
Several retiring Ministers have already said that to me today, but I won't let it happen.

01:26:24.730 --> 01:26:29.350
We've used money and technology to fight an unscrupulous system.

01:26:29.350 --> 01:26:31.830
It's no different from you with your guns.

01:26:31.830 --> 01:26:34.040
We hate crime.

01:26:34.040 --> 01:26:37.380
You breed criminals for the sake of profits.

01:26:38.210 --> 01:26:40.720
You'll understand one day.

01:27:33.430 --> 01:27:34.890
That's where you've been?

01:27:49.220 --> 01:27:50.740
You're late.

01:27:51.300 --> 01:27:53.200
She's just leaving.

01:28:22.280 --> 01:28:23.060
Kurutsu!

01:28:25.520 --> 01:28:27.460
Kurutsu is dead.

01:28:27.460 --> 01:28:32.530
Even controlling the same body,
 I can't behave with the same personality again.

01:28:33.660 --> 01:28:35.430
It's a mystery even to me.

01:28:36.470 --> 01:28:38.500
How long have you been doing that?

01:28:38.500 --> 01:28:40.380
Since the beginning.

01:28:40.380 --> 01:28:43.520
I've been compensating for the growth failure with micromachines,

01:28:43.520 --> 01:28:47.280
and though I can't be prosthetized,
 I've operated many prosthetic bodies.

01:28:48.280 --> 01:28:51.620
But you're the only one whose name I couldn't use.

01:28:51.620 --> 01:28:52.930
And Fire-Starter?

01:28:53.440 --> 01:28:55.410
Were you the developer?

01:29:07.760 --> 01:29:12.560
One day you'll understand the 
diversity of information packages,

01:29:12.560 --> 01:29:15.000
and the birth of a new world...

01:29:16.080 --> 01:29:19.540
I'm going there... Going where everyone else is.

01:29:53.420 --> 01:29:58.870
I pity you, remaining in a world like this when you were once freer than anyone.

01:30:29.330 --> 01:30:31.430
Did you get to say goodbye?

01:30:33.290 --> 01:30:35.230
Why did you use her?

01:30:36.390 --> 01:30:42.180
Two possibilities existed to avert the dead end of cyberbrains and prosthetic bodies.

01:30:42.180 --> 01:30:44.040
You and she were those possibilities.

01:30:44.660 --> 01:30:45.990
That's all.

01:30:47.280 --> 01:30:48.440
Take him.

01:30:52.230 --> 01:30:55.020
You should stop searching for the names of the dead.

01:30:55.020 --> 01:30:56.980
There's nothing to be gained.

01:30:56.980 --> 01:31:00.180
Take it from someone who's spent a long time as one of them.

01:31:05.450 --> 01:31:06.430
What is it?

01:31:06.430 --> 01:31:08.080
Won't you take us with you?

01:31:08.080 --> 01:31:10.130
Where should we go?!

01:31:10.130 --> 01:31:11.490
What do you want?

01:31:13.240 --> 01:31:20.070
To gain uniform standards by selling your bodies and 
Ghosts and sacrificing those who were given nothing?

01:31:21.020 --> 01:31:23.550
You all have cyberbrains.

01:31:23.550 --> 01:31:25.330
You have Ghosts you should be obeying.

01:31:26.230 --> 01:31:30.000
You seek more than that from other people—
what do you plan to offer in return?

01:31:31.390 --> 01:31:32.700
Build a future.

01:31:42.730 --> 01:31:44.620
It's just the government's "official position."

01:31:44.620 --> 01:31:47.240
It doesn't conflict with our trade.

01:31:47.240 --> 01:31:47.980
Excellent.

01:31:48.410 --> 01:31:53.480
When the slave state fails to serve, the aristocracy state starves.

01:31:53.810 --> 01:31:56.590
The slave trade benefits from labor shortages.

01:32:16.160 --> 01:32:18.270
You really gonna do this, Major?

01:32:34.320 --> 01:32:40.040
So, here we have the Far East Trade Representative, Vice-Minister of Commerce Itou, and some union officials.

01:32:40.040 --> 01:32:41.520
How dare you?

01:32:41.520 --> 01:32:44.880
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Defense Agency are watching this.

01:32:44.880 --> 01:32:50.560
I'll have Vice-Minister Itou here testify in a court of law about the Prime Minister's assassination.

01:32:50.560 --> 01:32:51.710
I'm ruined...

01:32:51.710 --> 01:32:53.150
Impossible.

01:32:53.150 --> 01:32:57.410
He applied for asylum and was accepted. He even signed the written oath.

01:32:57.410 --> 01:32:58.320
When?!

01:32:58.320 --> 01:32:59.920
I don't have to answer that.

01:32:59.920 --> 01:33:01.710
The papers are at the embassy.

01:33:01.710 --> 01:33:03.910
I'll forward them to you.

01:33:03.910 --> 01:33:06.320
The previous Prime Minister's wishes survive.

01:33:06.320 --> 01:33:07.680
You'll be assassinated.

01:33:07.680 --> 01:33:11.620
Ha! This is a civilized, pacifist nation.

01:33:11.620 --> 01:33:13.150
Oh, is it?

01:33:20.290 --> 01:33:21.280
Outside the window!

01:33:25.760 --> 01:33:27.030
Help!

01:33:27.030 --> 01:33:27.910
Hold your fire!

